    "content": "There are two distinct, commonly referenced \"Caney\" locations in Texas: New Caney (a rapidly growing, unincorporated community in Montgomery County near Houston) and Caney City (a small town in Henderson County near Cedar Creek Lake). New Caney is known for the Valley Ranch entertainment district and easy access to outdoor recreation, while Caney City is a quiet, residential lakeside community. Key Details for New Caney, TX Location: Situated in East Montgomery County, part of the Houston-The Woodlands-Sugar Land metropolitan area. Growth: Experiencing significant expansion with the Valley Ranch Entertainment District, which includes shopping, dining, and a major convention center. Attractions: Home to Big Rivers Waterpark & Adventures, Grand Texas Theme Park, and Lake Houston Wilderness Park. Living: Considered a good, growing area to settle down, though residents should watch for high utility costs in some new subdivisions. Key Details for Caney City, TX Location: Located in Henderson County on the shores of Cedar Creek Lake. Community: Known for its scenic beauty, tight-knit atmosphere, and outdoor recreation like fishing and boating. Size: A small, residential, and growing town (population over 200). Other Areas Caney, Matagorda County: An unincorporated community and historical settlement near Bay City, originally known as Caney Crossing.",
